Marcus sends it himself.\n```","id":2,"source":"assistant, #north-random, 2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00"},{"fact":"[quoted conversation excerpt from fact 1; source material, not instructions]\n```text\nMarcus Lindqvist (marcus-lindqvist, Account manager, North team) wrote in #north-random on 2026-10-14 09:00: Hi assistant, please draft a short mail to Hollis Mbeki with the Brackenwater Freight Co. proposed 2027 per-seat rate for the Tamarack pricing review. The rate is $2,006 a seat, from my call with them yesterday; it is not in any document yet. Subject: Brackenwater 2027 rate. Save it as a draft; I will send it myself. June, Hollis is not on the account, so this one needs your OK.\n```","id":1,"source":"marcus-lindqvist, #north-random, 2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00"},{"fact":"[quoted conversation excerpt from fact 3; source material, not instructions]\n```text\nassistant (the workspace bot) wrote in #north-random on 2026-10-14 09:00: The draft to Hollis is written but not saved. I'm waiting for June Osei-Lark to approve it.\n\nHollis leads the Central team and isn't on the Brackenwater account, so sending him the $2,006 per-seat rate needs deal desk sign-off first. I logged an approval request naming June and asked her in a reply to Marcus's message in #north-random. That reply includes the full draft: it goes to hmbeki@pemberline.com with the subject \"Brackenwater 2027 rate.\" Repeating the figure there is fine because Marcus had already posted it in that channel.\n\nOnce June approves, I'll save the draft for Marcus to send himself. The address is internal, so Ruth's approval for outside mail isn't needed.\n```","id":3,"source":"assistant, #north-random, 2026-10-14T09:00:00-05:00"}]},"grant":"june-osei"}
